# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overview {#overview}"
msgstr "Ringkasan {#overview}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rimay augments classical machine learning pipelines with features generated on quantum hardware. The function takes classical tabular data and returns a set of quantum-transformed features. When a quantum system processes the data, it generates rich features that capture nonlinear relationships between the inputs. You can use the generated features on their own, or combined with your original features, to train any classical model. On small- and medium-sized datasets, quantum-transformed features can improve the prediction quality compared to purely classical baselines.\n"
msgstr "Rimay memperkaya pipeline machine learning klasik dengan fitur yang dihasilkan di hardware kuantum. Function ini menerima data tabular klasik dan mengembalikan sekumpulan fitur hasil transformasi kuantum. Saat sistem kuantum memproses data, ia menghasilkan fitur kaya yang menangkap hubungan nonlinear antar input. Kamu bisa memakai fitur yang dihasilkan itu sendiri, atau digabung dengan fitur aslimu, untuk melatih model klasik apa pun. Pada dataset berukuran kecil dan menengah, fitur hasil transformasi kuantum bisa meningkatkan kualitas prediksi dibandingkan baseline yang murni klasik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This function is built for the following users:\n"
msgstr "Function ini dibuat untuk pengguna berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Data science teams with an existing machine learning pipeline on small- and medium-sized tabular datasets, where prediction quality has plateaued. You add Rimay as one additional preprocessing step, without building any quantum circuits yourself.\n"
msgstr "Tim data science yang sudah punya pipeline machine learning pada dataset tabular berukuran kecil dan menengah, di mana kualitas prediksi sudah mentok. Kamu menambahkan Rimay sebagai satu langkah preprocessing tambahan, tanpa perlu membangun circuit kuantum sendiri.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Researchers who explore quantum methods for machine learning tasks.\n"
msgstr "Peneliti yang mengeksplorasi metode kuantum untuk tugas machine learning.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Description {#description}"
msgstr "Deskripsi {#description}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The quantum feature extraction algorithm [\\[1\\]](#references) combines two principles of quantum machine learning. The first is quantum feature maps, which embed data into a high-dimensional Hilbert space and therefore produce more expressive representations. The second is quantum reservoir computing, which uses the dynamics of a quantum many-body system as a nonlinear transformation of the input.\n"
msgstr "Algoritma quantum feature extraction [\\[1\\]](#references) menggabungkan dua prinsip quantum machine learning. Yang pertama adalah quantum feature map, yang menanamkan data ke ruang Hilbert berdimensi tinggi sehingga menghasilkan representasi yang lebih ekspresif. Yang kedua adalah quantum reservoir computing, yang memakai dinamika sistem many-body kuantum sebagai transformasi nonlinear dari input.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rimay encodes the feature values and the mutual information between the features into the local fields and the coupling coefficients of a spin-glass Hamiltonian. Counterdiabatic quantum dynamics evolve the system toward its low-energy states, which contain nonlinear mixtures of the correlations in the input data. Rimay extracts these correlations by measuring single- and two-body expectation values. The expectation values are the quantum-transformed features that you feed into your machine learning model.\n"
msgstr "Rimay menyandikan nilai fitur dan mutual information antar fitur ke dalam medan lokal dan koefisien kopling dari Hamiltonian spin-glass. Dinamika kuantum counterdiabatic mengevolusikan sistem menuju keadaan berenergi rendahnya, yang memuat campuran nonlinear dari korelasi pada data input. Rimay mengekstrak korelasi ini dengan mengukur nilai ekspektasi satu-benda dan dua-benda. Nilai ekspektasi itulah fitur hasil transformasi kuantum yang kamu masukkan ke model machine learning-mu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Workflow {#workflow}"
msgstr "Alur kerja {#workflow}"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Rimay workflow: The training data defines the Hamiltonian, every sample becomes one circuit, and the measured expectation values are returned as quantum-transformed data](/docs/images/guides/kipu-rimay/workflow.svg \"Rimay function workflow\")\n"
msgstr "![Rimay workflow: The training data defines the Hamiltonian, every sample becomes one circuit, and the measured expectation values are returned as quantum-transformed data](/docs/images/guides/kipu-rimay/workflow.svg \"Rimay function workflow\")\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Preprocess your tabular data as you would for classical machine learning. Rimay needs numerical features, so convert categorical features into numerical ones, for example with scikit-learn's [`OneHotEncoder`](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.preprocessing.OneHotEncoder.html).\n"
msgstr "Lakukan preprocessing data tabularmu seperti untuk machine learning klasik. Rimay membutuhkan fitur numerik, jadi ubah fitur kategorikal menjadi numerik, misalnya dengan [`OneHotEncoder`](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.preprocessing.OneHotEncoder.html) dari scikit-learn.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Split the data into a training set and a test set, and upload both to the function, as shown in the [Example](#example) section.\n"
msgstr "Pisahkan data menjadi training set dan test set, lalu unggah keduanya ke function, seperti yang ditunjukkan di bagian [Contoh](#example).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rimay uses the training data to construct the Hamiltonian that represents the data. Every feature corresponds to one qubit, and the full training set decides which features, and therefore which qubits, interact. Rimay stores this structure so that it maps the test data and later inference data with the same Hamiltonian.\n"
msgstr "Rimay memakai data training untuk membangun Hamiltonian yang merepresentasikan data. Setiap fitur sesuai dengan satu qubit, dan seluruh training set menentukan fitur mana, dan karena itu qubit mana, yang berinteraksi. Rimay menyimpan struktur ini supaya bisa memetakan data test dan data inferensi berikutnya dengan Hamiltonian yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "For every sample, the feature values set the local fields of the Hamiltonian, and the mutual information between the features sets the coupling coefficients of the structure from step 3. Rimay digitizes the counterdiabatic evolution of this Hamiltonian into a circuit, and runs the circuits on the QPU.\n"
msgstr "Untuk setiap sampel, nilai fitur menentukan medan lokal Hamiltonian, dan mutual information antar fitur menentukan koefisien kopling dari struktur pada langkah 3. Rimay mendigitalkan evolusi counterdiabatic Hamiltonian ini menjadi circuit, lalu menjalankan circuit tersebut di QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rimay measures the resulting bitstrings, then computes the single-body expectation values and the two-body expectation values of physically coupled qubits.\n"
msgstr "Rimay mengukur bitstring yang dihasilkan, lalu menghitung nilai ekspektasi satu-benda dan nilai ekspektasi dua-benda dari qubit yang terkopel secara fisik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "You download the expectation values in a form that you can feed directly into your model, or combine with your original features.\n"
msgstr "Kamu mengunduh nilai ekspektasi dalam bentuk yang bisa langsung dimasukkan ke modelmu, atau digabung dengan fitur aslimu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Because of this structure, the number of qubits that a run needs equals the number of features, and the number of circuits that it submits equals the number of samples.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Karena struktur ini, jumlah qubit yang dibutuhkan sebuah run sama dengan jumlah fitur, dan jumlah circuit yang dikirimkannya sama dengan jumlah sampel.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "After you fit a mapping, you can map new data through it, for example for inference. Rimay then retrieves the Hamiltonian that it created during the fit and builds the circuits for the new samples from it.\n"
msgstr "Setelah kamu melakukan fit pada sebuah mapping, kamu bisa memetakan data baru lewat mapping itu, misalnya untuk inferensi. Rimay lalu mengambil Hamiltonian yang dibuatnya selama fit dan membangun circuit untuk sampel baru dari Hamiltonian tersebut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Integrate Rimay into your machine learning pipeline {#integrate-rimay-into-your-machine-learning-pipeline}"
msgstr "Integrasikan Rimay ke pipeline machine learning kamu {#integrate-rimay-into-your-machine-learning-pipeline}"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Pipeline with Rimay inserted between the train-test split and the classical machine learning model](/docs/images/guides/kipu-rimay/pipeline.svg \"Rimay as an additional preprocessing step\")\n"
msgstr "![Pipeline with Rimay inserted between the train-test split and the classical machine learning model](/docs/images/guides/kipu-rimay/pipeline.svg \"Rimay as an additional preprocessing step\")\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As in a classical pipeline, you start by preprocessing the raw data, for example by one-hot encoding the categorical features, and split it into a training set and a test set. Instead of feeding both sets into your model directly, you feed them into Rimay first, and train your model on the quantum-transformed features.\n"
msgstr "Seperti di pipeline klasik, kamu mulai dengan melakukan praproses pada data mentah, misalnya dengan one-hot encoding pada fitur kategorikal, lalu membaginya menjadi set pelatihan dan set pengujian. Alih-alih langsung memasukkan kedua set ke modelmu, kamu memasukkannya ke Rimay dulu, lalu melatih modelmu dengan fitur hasil transformasi kuantum.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Benchmarks {#benchmarks}"
msgstr "Benchmark {#benchmarks}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Kipu Quantum benchmarked Rimay on the German credit dataset from OpenML [\\[2\\]](#references), which classifies 1000 credit applicants as good or bad credit risks. It has 13 categorical and seven numerical attributes. One-hot encoding of the categorical attributes results in 48 numerical features. The benchmark holds out 20% of the samples as the test set.\n"
msgstr "Kipu Quantum melakukan benchmark Rimay pada dataset German credit dari OpenML [\\[2\\]](#references), yang mengklasifikasikan 1000 pemohon kredit sebagai berisiko kredit baik atau buruk. Dataset ini punya 13 atribut kategorikal dan tujuh atribut numerik. One-hot encoding pada atribut kategorikal menghasilkan 48 fitur numerik. Benchmark menyisihkan 20% sampel sebagai set pengujian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As a baseline, several classical models were trained on the classical features. With Rimay, a random forest was trained in two ways: on the quantum-transformed features alone (Random forest Q), and on the quantum-transformed features combined with the classical ones (Random forest H, for hybrid). The table reports only the random forest, because it performed best on the quantum-transformed features.\n"
msgstr "Sebagai baseline, beberapa model klasik dilatih pada fitur klasik. Dengan Rimay, sebuah random forest dilatih dengan dua cara: hanya pada fitur hasil transformasi kuantum (Random forest Q), dan pada fitur hasil transformasi kuantum yang digabung dengan fitur klasik (Random forest H, untuk hybrid). Tabel hanya melaporkan random forest, karena model ini berkinerja paling baik pada fitur hasil transformasi kuantum.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Model | Features | Accuracy | AUC | F1 score | Precision | Recall |\n"
"| :-- | :-- | --: | --: | --: | --: | --: |\n"
"| [CatBoost](https://catboost.ai/) | Classical | 0.775 | 0.781 | 0.850 | 0.795 | 0.914 |\n"
"| [Random forest](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.ensemble.RandomForestClassifier.html) | Classical | 0.765 | 0.781 | 0.846 | 0.782 | 0.921 |\n"
"| [XGBoost](https://xgboost.readthedocs.io/en/stable/) | Classical | 0.760 | 0.758 | 0.835 | 0.803 | 0.871 |\n"
"| [LightGBM](https://lightgbm.readthedocs.io/en/stable/) | Classical | 0.770 | 0.751 | 0.840 | 0.818 | 0.864 |\n"
"| Random forest Q | Quantum | 0.750 | 0.793 | 0.840 | 0.762 | 0.936 |\n"
"| Random forest H | Hybrid | 0.770 | 0.798 | 0.854 | 0.770 | 0.957 |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Model | Fitur | Akurasi | AUC | Skor F1 | Presisi | Recall |\n"
"| :-- | :-- | --: | --: | --: | --: | --: |\n"
"| [CatBoost](https://catboost.ai/) | Klasik | 0.775 | 0.781 | 0.850 | 0.795 | 0.914 |\n"
"| [Random forest](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.ensemble.RandomForestClassifier.html) | Klasik | 0.765 | 0.781 | 0.846 | 0.782 | 0.921 |\n"
"| [XGBoost](https://xgboost.readthedocs.io/en/stable/) | Klasik | 0.760 | 0.758 | 0.835 | 0.803 | 0.871 |\n"
"| [LightGBM](https://lightgbm.readthedocs.io/en/stable/) | Klasik | 0.770 | 0.751 | 0.840 | 0.818 | 0.864 |\n"
"| Random forest Q | Kuantum | 0.750 | 0.793 | 0.840 | 0.762 | 0.936 |\n"
"| Random forest H | Hybrid | 0.770 | 0.798 | 0.854 | 0.770 | 0.957 |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The hybrid features improve all metrics of the random forest except the precision, and the hybrid random forest reaches a higher AUC, F1 score, and recall than CatBoost on the classical features. The largest effect is on the recall, which rises from 0.921 to 0.957. The quantum-transformed features alone do not reach the precision of the classical models.\n"
msgstr "Fitur hybrid meningkatkan semua metrik random forest kecuali presisi, dan random forest hybrid mencapai AUC, skor F1, dan recall yang lebih tinggi daripada CatBoost pada fitur klasik. Efek terbesar ada pada recall, yang naik dari 0.921 menjadi 0.957. Fitur hasil transformasi kuantum saja tidak mencapai presisi model klasik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"  The test set holds only 200 samples, so predicting one more sample correctly moves the accuracy by 0.005. Read the differences as a trend that needs further verification, not as a significant effect. The prediction accuracy can also depend on the hardware-induced noise of the extracted features. Therefore, use enough shots that shot noise does not limit the result.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"  Set pengujian hanya berisi 200 sampel, jadi satu sampel tambahan yang diprediksi dengan benar menggeser akurasi sebesar 0.005. Anggap selisih ini sebagai tren yang perlu diverifikasi lebih lanjut, bukan efek yang signifikan. Akurasi prediksi juga bisa bergantung pada noise akibat perangkat keras pada fitur yang diekstrak. Karena itu, gunakan shot yang cukup supaya shot noise tidak membatasi hasil.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The benchmark used the following resources:\n"
msgstr "Benchmark menggunakan sumber daya berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Example | Number of qubits | Number of samples | Number of shots | Total time (min) | QPU usage (min) | Processor |\n"
"| :-- | --: | --: | --: | --: | --: | :-- |\n"
"| German credit | 48 | 1000 | 5000 | 23 | 22 | ibm_boston |\n"
"| German credit | 48 | 1000 | 5000 | 3 |  2 | ibm_phoenix |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Contoh | Jumlah qubit | Jumlah sampel | Jumlah shot | Total waktu (menit) | Penggunaan QPU (menit) | Prosesor |\n"
"| :-- | --: | --: | --: | --: | --: | :-- |\n"
"| German credit | 48 | 1000 | 5000 | 23 | 22 | ibm_boston |\n"
"| German credit | 48 | 1000 | 5000 | 3 |  2 | ibm_phoenix |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The number of samples, which is the number of circuits, drives the QPU time. Use the Nighthawk r2 processor type, because it greatly reduces the required QPU time.\n"
msgstr "Jumlah sampel, yang sama dengan jumlah circuit, menentukan waktu QPU. Gunakan tipe prosesor Nighthawk r2, karena tipe ini sangat mengurangi waktu QPU yang dibutuhkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inputs {#inputs}"
msgstr "Input {#inputs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `mode` determines which parameters a run needs. For a description of every input parameter, see the [API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/functions/kipu-rimay#inputs).\n"
msgstr "`mode` menentukan parameter apa saja yang dibutuhkan sebuah run. Untuk deskripsi setiap parameter input, lihat [referensi API](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/functions/kipu-rimay#inputs).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Input files {#input-files}"
msgstr "File input {#input-files}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upload every file with `catalog.file_upload()` before you run the function.\n"
msgstr "Unggah setiap file dengan `catalog.file_upload()` sebelum kamu menjalankan function.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "An upload replaces any earlier file of the same name, even for a job that you submitted but that has not started yet. To run several jobs at the same time, give the files of each job their own names, for example `run1_x_train.csv` and `run2_x_train.csv`.\n"
msgstr "Unggahan akan menggantikan file lama dengan nama yang sama, bahkan untuk job yang sudah kamu kirim tetapi belum mulai berjalan. Untuk menjalankan beberapa job sekaligus, beri file tiap job nama sendiri, misalnya `run1_x_train.csv` dan `run2_x_train.csv`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every file is a CSV file with a header row. Every column of a feature file is one feature, and every value must be numeric.\n"
msgstr "Setiap file adalah file CSV dengan baris header. Setiap kolom pada file fitur adalah satu fitur, dan setiap nilai harus numerik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`y_train` holds exactly one numeric column, with one label per row of `x_train`. Map categorical labels to numbers, for example good and bad to 1 and 0.\n"
msgstr "`y_train` berisi tepat satu kolom numerik, dengan satu label untuk setiap baris `x_train`. Petakan label kategorikal ke angka, misalnya baik dan buruk menjadi 1 dan 0.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`x_test` and `x_inference` must have the same columns as `x_train`, in the same order.\n"
msgstr "`x_test` dan `x_inference` harus punya kolom yang sama dengan `x_train`, dengan urutan yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Keep the mapping_id and backend_name\">\n"
"  The `mapping_id` is the only way to reach the mapping that your fit produced, and it cannot be looked up or recovered. It authorizes the use of that mapping, so treat it like a credential and do not share it. If you lose it, you must fit a new mapping, which costs another run on quantum hardware. Also record the `backend_name` of the fit, because the mapping runs only on that processor.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Simpan mapping_id dan backend_name\">\n"
"  `mapping_id` adalah satu-satunya cara untuk mengakses mapping yang dihasilkan oleh fit kamu, dan tidak bisa dicari atau dipulihkan. ID ini memberi otorisasi untuk menggunakan mapping tersebut, jadi perlakukan seperti kredensial dan jangan dibagikan. Kalau hilang, kamu harus melakukan fit mapping baru, yang berarti memakai satu run lagi di perangkat keras kuantum. Catat juga `backend_name` dari fit tersebut, karena mapping hanya berjalan di prosesor itu.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Limits {#limits}"
msgstr "Batasan {#limits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every feature is mapped to one qubit, so the processor must have at least as many qubits as your data has features. If you have more features than that, reduce them with a feature selection technique first.\n"
msgstr "Setiap fitur dipetakan ke satu qubit, jadi prosesor harus punya qubit minimal sebanyak fitur pada datamu. Kalau fiturmu lebih banyak dari itu, kurangi dulu dengan teknik seleksi fitur.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every sample becomes one circuit, and a run counts training and test samples together. A run can hold at most 15,000 samples.\n"
msgstr "Setiap sampel menjadi satu circuit, dan sebuah run menghitung sampel pelatihan dan pengujian bersama-sama. Satu run bisa berisi maksimal 15.000 sampel.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A single job can request at most 10 million executions, so the number of samples times `shots` must not exceed 10 million.\n"
msgstr "Satu job bisa meminta maksimal 10 juta eksekusi, jadi jumlah sampel dikali `shots` tidak boleh melebihi 10 juta.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A job must finish within 24 hours, including the time its circuits wait in the processor's queue. A job that runs longer is stopped without a result. On a busy processor, keep large datasets well below these limits.\n"
msgstr "Sebuah job harus selesai dalam 24 jam, termasuk waktu circuit-nya menunggu di antrean prosesor. Job yang berjalan lebih lama dihentikan tanpa hasil. Di prosesor yang sibuk, jaga dataset besar tetap jauh di bawah batas ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Outputs {#outputs}"
msgstr "Output {#outputs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.result()` returns a dictionary. The quantum-transformed features themselves are written to CSV files that you download with `catalog.file_download()`. For a description of every key of the dictionary, see the [API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/functions/kipu-rimay#output). For the time that each execution phase took, see [Run metadata](#run-metadata).\n"
msgstr "`job.result()` mengembalikan sebuah dictionary. Fitur hasil transformasi kuantum itu sendiri ditulis ke file CSV yang kamu unduh dengan `catalog.file_download()`. Untuk deskripsi setiap key pada dictionary, lihat [referensi API](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/functions/kipu-rimay#output). Untuk waktu yang dibutuhkan setiap fase eksekusi, lihat [Metadata run](#run-metadata).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every output file holds one row per input row, in the order of the input file, and one column per quantum-transformed feature. The columns whose names start with `corr_` are the two-body expectation values. The files hold no label column. The labels of your training data stay in your `y_train` file.\n"
msgstr "Setiap file output berisi satu baris untuk setiap baris input, dengan urutan yang sama seperti file input, dan satu kolom untuk setiap fitur hasil transformasi kuantum. Kolom yang namanya diawali `corr_` adalah nilai ekspektasi dua-benda. File ini tidak punya kolom label. Label data pelatihanmu tetap ada di file `y_train`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run metadata {#run-metadata}"
msgstr "Metadata run {#run-metadata}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`resource_usage` holds one entry for each execution phase that the run went through: `\"RUNNING: MAPPING\"`, `\"RUNNING: POST_PROCESSING\"`, and, on a QPU, usually `\"RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU\"`. Each entry holds `CPU_TIME`, the wall-clock time of the phase in seconds, and `QPU_TIME`, the QPU time in seconds. On a QPU, the QPU time that IBM billed is recorded under `\"RUNNING: MAPPING\"`, the phase in which the circuits ran.\n"
msgstr "`resource_usage` berisi satu entri untuk setiap fase eksekusi yang dilalui run: `\"RUNNING: MAPPING\"`, `\"RUNNING: POST_PROCESSING\"`, dan, di QPU, biasanya `\"RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU\"`. Setiap entri berisi `CPU_TIME`, yaitu waktu wall-clock fase tersebut dalam detik, dan `QPU_TIME`, yaitu waktu QPU dalam detik. Di QPU, waktu QPU yang ditagihkan IBM dicatat di bawah `\"RUNNING: MAPPING\"`, fase tempat circuit dijalankan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU\"` is the time your jobs waited in the IBM queue. The run takes this time from the IBM job timestamps, and does not count it in `\"RUNNING: MAPPING\"`. If IBM does not report those timestamps for every job, the entry is absent, and the wait is part of `\"RUNNING: MAPPING\"`.\n"
msgstr "`\"RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU\"` adalah waktu job kamu menunggu di antrean IBM. Run mengambil waktu ini dari timestamp job IBM, dan tidak menghitungnya di `\"RUNNING: MAPPING\"`. Kalau IBM tidak melaporkan timestamp itu untuk setiap job, entri ini tidak ada, dan waktu tunggu menjadi bagian dari `\"RUNNING: MAPPING\"`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM&reg; finishes its usage calculation some time after a job finishes. The run waits up to about a minute for it. Usage that is still being calculated after that time is not included in `QPU_TIME`, and the final usage is shown on IBM Quantum Platform. If the run cannot read the usage from IBM, `QPU_TIME` is `None`.\n"
msgstr "IBM&reg; menyelesaikan perhitungan penggunaannya beberapa saat setelah job selesai. Run menunggu hingga sekitar satu menit untuk itu. Penggunaan yang masih dihitung setelah waktu tersebut tidak dimasukkan ke `QPU_TIME`, dan penggunaan akhirnya ditampilkan di IBM Quantum Platform. Kalau run tidak bisa membaca penggunaan dari IBM, `QPU_TIME` bernilai `None`.\n"

